<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Upbeat Howden Africa lifts first-half shr.</title>
<headline>Upbeat Howden Africa lifts first-half shr.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended October 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     20.05	 vs 18.66</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  4.00</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   11.63	 vs   9.33</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   17.87	 vs  13.77</p>
<p>    Tax			  5.02	 vs   3.99</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    0.84	 vs   0.72</p>
<p>    Operating profit	17.03	 vs  14.49</p>
<p>    Turnover		 208.68	 vs 148.95</p>
<p>Div payable to shareholders on register January 24</p>
<p>Full name: Howden Africa Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it would offer capitalisation shares in lieu of the cash dividend. Details will be published on January 20.</p>
<p>The specialist air and gas handling equipment group, which listed on the Johannesburg Stock Exchange earlier this year, said order intake had increased by 136 percent over the period. Managing director Jan Moodie said this provided a solid base for a good financial performance in the second half.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
